@restregular/dsh-visual-browser README · Native controls: the parts that are not page content：Some controls are drawn by the browser or the operating system, so they never
appear in a picture and CDP input never reaches them. The plugin writes the
value instead of pretending to click:

@restregular/dsh-visual-browser README · Looking like an ordinary browser：A page can tell a driven browser apart, and sites that bind a session to the
browser they handed it to kill that session once they see it. With `stealth:
true` (the default) the command line is built so the page sees a normal Chrome:
